gnee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in: v4.4.1\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf a parameter of a static function has the same name as a member variable, the editor issues a shadowing warning:\n\n> W 0:00:01:212   The local function parameter \"bar\" is shadowing an already-declared variable at line 3 in the current class.\n  <GDScript Error>SHADOWED_VARIABLE\n  <GDScript Source>node.gd:5\n\n\n\nHowever, the function parameter is not shadowing the member variable; since the function is static, member variables are out of scope, and so no shadowing occurs. It does not seem like this warning should trigger in this instance.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```python\nvar bar # bar1\n\nstatic func foo(bar): # bar2\n\tpass # Here, bar2 is in scope, but bar1 is out of scope. Therefore, no shadowing occurs.\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[shadowing.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20747502/shadowing.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"h